name>Brown</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sprouting of motor nerves in adult muscle: a recapitulation ontogeny</article-title><source>Trends Neurosci</source><year>1984</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>10</fpage><lpage>14</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Budnik</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhong</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>C-W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Morphological plasticity of motor axons in Drosophila mutants with altered excitability</article-title><source>J Neurosci</source><year>1990</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>3754</fpage><lpage>3768</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1700086</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other">Caroni, P. 1997. Overexpression of growth-associated proteins in the neurons  of adult transgenic mice. <italic>J. Neurosci. Methods.</italic> In press.</citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Caroni</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The downregulation of growth-associated proteins in motoneurons at the onset of synapse elimination is controlled by muscle activity and IGF1</article-title><source>J Neurosci</source><year>1992</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>3849</fpage><lpage>3861</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1328560</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Caroni</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Schneider</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiefer</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Zapf</surname><given-names>J</given-names></